      "reasons": [
        "The packet only supports a narrow, context-specific use: an ‘emotionally pleasant internal object’ used as the target of attentional shift, not a general definition of ‘internal object’ as any mental focus contrasted with the outside environment.",
        "The phrase ‘emotionally pleasant mental focus’ is too broad as a definition of the term; in the packet, pleasantness appears only as the example ‘a positive memory’ within a proposed intervention, not as an inherent property of all internal objects.",
        "The definition implies a general cognitive term sense, but the source uses the phrase in a sleep-paralysis treatment proposal rather than establishing a standard dictionary meaning."
